drm/amd/display: VRR through a DP-to-HDMI PCON from the HF-VSDB alone

Rewritten for cachyos-7.4-rc1-1, where amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps()
changed under the 7.3 version of this patch:

* the AMD VSDB is now parsed in software by the DRM core
  (display_info.amd_vsdb, get_amd_vsdb()), so DCN201's missing DMUB and
  DMCU no longer keep a PCON from its AMD VSDB range;
* upstream now falls back to the HDMI 2.1 VRR range from the HF-VSDB for
  every sink without a FreeSync range, which is what the 7.3 patch added
  for the PCON;
* and a new rule turns FreeSync off for HDMI and for an allowlisted PCON
  whose sink has no MCCS VCP code, which only comes from an AMD VSDB.

A TV with HDMI Forum VRR and no AMD VSDB (an LG G5 carries only the HDMI
and HF-VSDB blocks) behind an allowlisted PCON such as the CH7218 now
gets its range from upstream's fallback, but not the SDP v1.3 packing and
adaptive-sync type the PCON path needs, and the VCP rule then turns
FreeSync off again. So for exactly that case (no AMD VSDB, PCON in the
allowlist, FreeSync range found, HF-VSDB VRR advertised) set
pack_sdp_v1_3 and the adaptive-sync type as the AMD VSDB path does, and
keep the VCP rule from undoing it. Everything else is upstream's.

Logs "VRR: PCON HF-VSDB fallback: ..." at drm_dbg_driver level next to
the existing "VRR:" lines, so drm.debug=0x2 shows the decision.

---
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 24 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index c9d56d38d423..755dd5664b14 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -3757,6 +3757,7 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	struct amdgpu_hdmi_vsdb_info vsdb_info = {0};
 	const struct edid *edid;
 	bool freesync_capable = false;
+	bool pcon_hf_vrr = false;
 	enum adaptive_sync_type as_type = ADAPTIVE_SYNC_TYPE_NONE;
 
 	if (!connector->state) {
@@ -3916,6 +3917,27 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A DP-to-HDMI PCON in the allowlist whose sink has no AMD VSDB but
+	 * HDMI Forum VRR (an LG G5 carries only the HDMI and HF-VSDB blocks):
+	 * the HF-VSDB fallback above found the range, but the PCON still
+	 * needs the SDP v1.3 packing and its adaptive-sync type, as the AMD
+	 * VSDB path sets them. Without an AMD VSDB there is no MCCS VCP code
+	 * either, so the rule below must not turn it off.
+	 */
+	if (!has_vsdb && as_type == FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST && freesync_capable &&
+	    connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.supported) {
+		amdgpu_dm_connector->pack_sdp_v1_3 = true;
+		amdgpu_dm_connector->as_type = as_type;
+		pcon_hf_vrr = true;
+		drm_dbg_driver(adev_to_drm(adev),
+			       "VRR: PCON HF-VSDB fallback: vrr_cap[min=%d max=%d] -> min=%d max=%d\n",
+			       connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.vrr_min,
+			       connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.vrr_max,
+			       amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq,
+			       amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq);
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Apply per-monitor FreeSync range quirks. Some panels report a
 	 * VRR minimum that does not operate reliably; force it when the
@@ -3931,7 +3953,7 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	/* HDMI/PCON without an EDID FreeSync VCP code is not FreeSync-capable. */
 	if ((sink->sink_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_HDMI_TYPE_A ||
 	     as_type == FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST) &&
-	    !sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code)
+	    !sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code && !pcon_hf_vrr)
 		freesync_capable = false;
 
 	/* Handle MCCS */
